  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 259 AM EDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nMid-level ridging will begin to build on Wednesday night as the mid-\nlevel impulse gets dragged northward with the mean flow. Near the \nsurface, high pressure will continue to build across the western \nAtlantic into the weekend, bringing the return of easterly to \nsoutheasterly flow across the area. Moisture advection will \ncontinue, with PWATs forecast to continue hovering near 2 inches \nthrough the period. This pattern will promote continued scattered to \nwidespread shower and thunderstorm development each afternoon. Storm \nactivity will likely favor interior and southwestern Florida due to \nthe stronger easterly flow during the latter half of the week. \nConditions could become a bit windy as well towards the weekend as a \nfrontal boundary settles across the southeastern US; its proximity \nto the surface high will help tighten up the pressure gradient \nacross the region.\n\nThere is increasing confidence that temperatures will increase back \ninto the upper 80s and low 90s areawide over the weekend, especially \nas easterly flow and moisture return increase.",
